WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.075
Who decides?

2
00:00:01.075 --> 00:00:05.669
The decision record, from the guide's
Step 1, scopes each run: the tenant,

3
00:00:05.669 --> 00:00:10.988
the pillars, and the Azure subscriptions
for the infrastructure pillar; the run

4
00:00:10.988 --> 00:00:16.387
account; the cadence; the pinned tool version;
telemetry; and where the output goes.

5
00:00:16.387 --> 00:00:17.862
The see-so approves it.

6
00:00:17.862 --> 00:00:21.510
Then each pillar owner reads
their own tab, with the filters,

7
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.860
and notes every investigate,
skipped and error result,

8
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:29.326
and every failed result whose feature
may not exist in the tenant's cloud.

9
00:00:29.326 --> 00:00:35.538
For a G C C tenant, the workbook's baseline,
the tool uses the worldwide endpoints.

10
00:00:35.538 --> 00:00:39.163
In G C C High and D O D,
there's a case to know.

11
00:00:39.163 --> 00:00:42.731
Learn's Exchange Online service
description says anti-phishing

12
00:00:42.731 --> 00:00:47.025
impersonation protection and spoof
intelligence aren't yet available there.

13
00:00:47.025 --> 00:00:51.222
So a failed impersonation test in
those clouds is a boundary finding,

14
00:00:51.222 --> 00:00:53.780
not a configuration change to make today.
